 "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe past experiences in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About the Past "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the Simple Past tense to talk about the past events."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">a particular time in the past</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">arrived</span> home at six o'clock.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">continued for some time in the past</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Everybody <span class=\\\"strong\\\">worked</span> hard to complete the job.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">several times in the past </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Most weekends we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">stayed</span> at home and played video games.</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are       finished.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.   </br>   Regular verbs end in -ed or -ied.    </br></br>  Irregular verbs change in different ways.  </br>    For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary did followed by      the verb in the base form, like Did you ask \u2026 ?  </br>    Did is the past form of to do.   "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "already"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do something before"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I already miss them and I haven't even left yet."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le08ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about tourist activities."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "memory"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to past events in your mind for a long time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My friends and I have lovely memories of our childhoods."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le08ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hang out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spend time together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you want to hang out later?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le08ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sad"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be upset, unhappy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sally is a little sad."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le08ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "itinerary "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the details of a trip"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Last night, I printed out the full itinerary. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le08ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Don't get me wrong"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Do not misunderstand me"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Don't get me wrong, I love to travel."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le08ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le08ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The simple past is used to talk about a completed action in a time before now. The time of the action can be in the recent past or the distant past. <br />For the\u00a0<span class=\"strong\">negative</span>\u00a0and\u00a0<span class=\"strong\">interrogative</span>\u00a0forms of all verbs in the simple past, always use the auxiliary\u00a0<span class=\"strong\">did</span>.\u00a0<br />Look at the chart to review the Simple Past tense in its different forms:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Affirmative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative<span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Interrogative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + verb + ed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + did not  + infinitive without to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Did + subject + infinitive without to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">realized</span> that I would be away from my friends.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">did not realize</span> that I would be away from my friends.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Did</span> she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">realize</span> that I would be away from my friends?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, make a list of 5 things you miss the most when you traveled."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Put them in order from 1-5. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 5 sentences from your notes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Simple Past tense. For example: <span class=\"italic\">I missed my friends.</span>"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I put ideas in order from 1-5."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write 5 sentences of five things I miss the most."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use past simple tense in sentences."}]}], "type": "sena"}